course: dictionary
lesson: 779
title: Beautify: making things prettier
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Beautify is a doing word, which is a verb. To beautify something is to make it more beautiful. «Beautify the school garden» means make it look nicer, perhaps with new flowers and bright paint.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. In Alice's story, the Gryphon asks if she knows what «beautify» is. Alice thinks hard and says «it means—to—make—anything—prettier». She has guessed well, and the dictionary agrees.
explain: Opposites can also help. Alice guesses that «uglify» must mean the opposite of beautify. If beautify means make prettier, then uglify means make uglier. Always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: does it still make sense?
fact: Beautify is a verb, so it changes form: beautify, beautifies, beautified, beautifying.
fact: «Beautify» means to make something more beautiful.
fact: People can beautify a town with flowers, or with murals, which are big paintings on walls.
fact: «Beautified» is the past form, so it tells you something was made prettier in the past.
fact: «Uglify» is the opposite of beautify: it means to make something uglier.
exercise: «The children decided to beautify the school garden.» What does beautify mean here? | Leave it dark and cold | Dig it up and throw it away | Make it smaller | *Make it look nicer
exercise: Which form of beautify is in this sentence? «Maya beautified the hall with paper flowers.» | beautify | beautifying | beautifies | *beautified
exercise: Alice guesses «uglify» means the opposite of beautify. Which meaning fits? | Make something bigger | Make something cleaner | *Make something uglier | Make something quieter
test: «Before the ball, she beautified herself with a new dress and a ribbon.» What does beautified mean? | Ran away quickly | *Made herself look more beautiful | Made herself tired | Asked for help
test: In «the community painted murals to beautify the old bus station», what are they trying to do? | Make the station quieter | Move the station to a new place | *Make the station look nicer | Close the station for good
exam: Choose the sentence where beautify is used as a verb. | *They plan to beautify the square with flowers | The beauty of the square was lost | The beautify was lovely | Beautify is a long word
